extends main

block pre
  #website.clearfix
    include domains/foreside/header
    .inner
      .page.partner.foreside(data-id="partners/foreside")
        .col
          h2.partner_logo
            a(href="http://foreside.com/", target="_blank") Foreside 
          h3 Sponsor/Advisor
          a.site_link(href="http://foreside.com/", target="_blank") www.foreside.com
        .col2 Foreside serves separate account managers and the sponsors of open-end, closed-end, exchange traded and alternative investment funds, including commodity pools, with Sarbanes-Oxley, independent CCO, CCO support, registered representative, and active and statutory distribution services.  Today, Foreside employs more than 80 experienced professionals including securities attorneys, certified public accountants and key fund officers.  Foreside acts as distributor for over 70 registrants with AUM of over $500 billion, and maintains over 6,000 dealer agreements and over 140 exchange-traded product AP Agreements.  Foreside has provided services to Investment Advisers, Broker-Dealers, CPOs/CTAs, Mutual Funds, Hedge Funds, Private Equity Funds, and Investment Bankers.
      .page.partner.ise(data-id="partners/ise")
        .col
          h2.partner_logo
            a(href="http://www.ise.com/", target="_blank") International Securities Exchange 
          h3 Index Provider
          a.site_link(href="http://www.ise.com/", target="_blank") www.ise.com
        .col2 The International Securities Exchange (ISE) was the first all-electronic options exchange, beginning operations in May, 2000.  The ISE was acquired by the Deutsche Borse AG (DBAG) in 2007 for $2.8B.  DBAG has an $11B market cap.  With 215 employees, ISE revenue in 2010 was $230M.  Its E&O is covered under DBAGs Comprehensive Crime & Dishonesty Insurance (CCDI).  It maintained a €20M policy with Lloyds.  The SEC is a registered and regulated securities exchange with over 150 member firms more than 30 of which are major US broker-dealers and market makers including Goldman Sachs, Citigroup, Citadel, Merrill Lynch, Morgan Stanley, JP Morgan, UBS and Credit Suisse.  Domestic Equity, Global Equity, Future-based, options-based, and FX-based indexes are the basis for ETPs.
      .page.partner.state_street(data-id="partners/statestreet")
        .col
          h2.partner_logo
            a(href="http://www.statestreet.com/", target="_blank") State Street
          h3 State Street
          a.site_link(href="http://statestreet.com/", target="_blank") www.statestreet.com
        .col2
          p State Street is one of the world's leading providers of financial services to institutional investors including investment servicing, investment management and investment research and trading.  With US $23.4-trillion in assets under custody and administration, and US $2.1trillion* under management as of September 30, 2012 State Street operates in 29 countries and more than 100 geographic markets.  State Street pioneered ETF servicing as the service provider for the first ETF product launched in the US in 1993. State Street has consistently been positioned at the top of industry rankings.  It was named Best Online Bank among FX trading systems (Currenex), No. 1 US institutional tax-exempt assets, No. 1 servicer of alternative assets globally, No. 1 servicer of retail assets globally, No. 1 servicer of equity assets globally, No. 1 servicer of hedge fund assets globally, as well as being named The Most Recognized ETF Brand.
          p *This AUM includes assets of SPDR Gold Trust (approximately $75.3 billion as of September 30, 2012) for which State Street Global Markets, LLC an affiliate of State Street Global Advisors serves as the marketing agent.
        
      .page.partner.kl_gates(data-id="partners/klgates")
        .col
          h2.partner_logo
            a(href="http://www.klgates.com/", target="_blank") K&L Gates 
          h3 K&L Gates's Role 
          a.site_link(href="http://klgates.com/", target="_blank") www.klgates.com
        .col2
          p K&L Gates is one of the premier Investment Management practices in the United States.  K&L Gates is comprised of more than 2,000 lawyers who practice in 46 different office located on five continents: Anchorage, Austin, Beijing, Berlin, Boston, Brisbane, Brussels, Charleston, Charlotte, Chicago, Dallas, Doha, Dubai, Fort Worth, Frankfurt, Harrisburg, Hong Kong, London, Los Angeles, Melbourne, Miami, Milan, Moscow, Newark, New York, Orange County, Palo Alto, Paris, Perth, Pittsburgh, Portland, Raleigh, Research Triangle Park, San Diego, San Francisco, Sao Paulo, Seattle, Seoul, Shanghai, Singapore, Spokane, Sydney, Taipei, Tokyo, Warsaw, and Washington.
          p K&L Gates represents leading global corporations, growth and middle market companies, capital markets participants and entrepreneurs in every major industry group as well as public sector entities, educational institutions, philanthropic organizations and individuals.  Our practice is a robust full market practice – cutting edge, complex and dynamic, at once regional, national and international in scope.  Over each of the last four years our revenues exceeded $1 Billion and, as stated in the July 2010 issue of the UK Publication Legal Business, the firm "has further cemented its position as the Global 100s fastest growing firm."

      .page.partner.two-n(data-id="partners/two-n")
        .col
          h2.partner_logo
            a(href="http://two-n.com/", target="_blank") Two-N, Inc. 
          h3 ETF Mapper
          a.site_link(href="http://two-n.com/", target="_blank") www.two-n.com
        .col2 Two-N, Inc. is a New York Based design studio specializing in design and development of data visualizations. We work with our clients and their diverse – and often complex – datasets to produce interactive applications, data displays, user interface designs, and infographics. Our design philosophy promotes experimentation, innovation and process adaptability throughout the lifecycle of any project. Two-N has been engaged in a number of exciting data visualization projects, ranging from financial trading data to economic data, demographic data, and other complex data sets across a number of leading organizations, including Bloomberg LP, The New York Stock Exchange, SAP, WNYC, and Google Labs.


